iovcnt → Number of buffers in the array
2️⃣ What it does

writev() writes multiple buffers to a file (or socket) in a single system call:

The kernel looks at each iov[i].iov_base and iov[i].iov_len
Writes all bytes from all buffers sequentially to the file descriptor fd
Returns the total number of bytes written
This is more efficient than multiple write() calls, because:

Only one system call
Guarantees atomicity (no other process can write between buffers)

