1️⃣ What 0644 means
Linux file permissions are expressed in octal numbers (0xxx).
The 3 least significant digits represent owner, group, and others.
0 6 4 4
| | | |
| | | +-- Others (everyone else) → 4 = read only
| | +---- Group → 4 = read only
| +------ Owner → 6 = read + write
+-------- Leading 0 = octal number

2️⃣ Breaking it down
6 → owner permissions → 4 + 2 = read + write
4 → group permissions → read only
4 → others → read only

So the file permissions are:

-rw-r--r--
r = read
w = write
x = execute (not set here)

Owner: read/write
Group: read only
Others: read only



